---
/** Chart 4: network latency by path, on a log scale (0.18 to 23.4 ms cannot be read linearly). */
const x = (ms: number) => 160 + 179.19 * Math.log10(ms / 0.1);
const major = [0.1, 1, 10];
const minor = [0.2, 0.5, 2, 5, 20];
const blocks = [
	{
		t: 44,
		l1: 'Wired 2.5GbE',
		l2: 'direct UDP · 1100 B',
		tone: '#4CD69B',
		rtt: [0.18, 0.25] as const,
		p50: 0.99,
		p99: 7.3,
		foot: 'ceiling 150 Mbps sustained · 1173 B on the wire',
	},
	{
		t: 188,
		l1: 'Tailscale direct',
		l2: 'WireGuard · 1100 B',
		tone: '#FF7A1F',
		rtt: [0.33, 0.4] as const,
		p50: 3.15,
		p99: 23.4,
		foot: 'ceiling 100 Mbps direct, 20 Mbps relay · 1233 B on the wire (+5.1%)',
	},
];
const wifi = { t: 116, lo: 4.4, hi: 8.4 };
const wc = wifi.t + 36;
const label =
	'Network latency by path, log scale. Wired 2.5GbE direct UDP: p50 0.99 ms, p99 7.3 ms at 100 Mbps. Wi-Fi 6: p50 between 4.4 and 8.4 ms across runs, no p99 published. Tailscale direct: p50 3.15 ms, p99 23.4 ms at 100 Mbps.';
---

<figure class="chart">
	<div class="diagram" style="--min: 640px" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Transport path chart, scrolls sideways">
		<svg viewBox="0 0 696 280" width="696" height="280" role="img" aria-label={label} class="svg-mono">
			<g class="grid" shape-rendering="crispEdges">
				{minor.map((v) => <path d={`M${x(v)} 40 V254`} stroke="#F2EFEA0D" stroke-width="1" />)}
				{major.map((v) => <path d={`M${x(v)} 40 V254`} stroke="#F2EFEA1A" stroke-width="1" />)}
				<path d="M160 254 H604" stroke="#2C3038" stroke-width="1"></path>
				<path d="M0 36 H696" stroke="#F2EFEA14" stroke-width="1"></path>
			</g>
			<text x="0" y="26" font-size="10" letter-spacing="0.6" fill="#8C919B">RAW AEAD UDP BURST · WIRED AND TAILSCALE AT 100 Mbps</text>
			<text x="696" y="26" font-size="10" letter-spacing="0.6" fill="#6E7480" text-anchor="end">p50 / p99 · ms</text>
			<text x="0" y="268" font-size="9.5" fill="#6E7480">LOG SCALE</text>
			{
				major.map((v) => (
					<text x={x(v)} y="268" font-size="10" fill="#6E7480" text-anchor="middle">
						{v}
					</text>
				))
			}

			{
				blocks.map((b) => {
					const yc = b.t + 36;
					return (
						<g>
							<text x="0" y={b.t + 22} font-size="11" font-weight="600" fill="#F2EFEA">
								{b.l1}
							</text>
							<text x="0" y={b.t + 36} font-size="9.5" fill="#8C919B">
								{b.l2}
							</text>
							<rect x={x(b.rtt[0])} y={b.t + 8} width={x(b.rtt[1]) - x(b.rtt[0])} height="4" rx="2" fill="#6E7480" />
							<text x={x(b.rtt[1]) + 8} y={b.t + 13} font-size="9" fill="#6E7480">
								min RTT {b.rtt[0].toFixed(2)}–{b.rtt[1].toFixed(2)}
							</text>
							<rect x={x(b.p50)} y={yc - 7} width={x(b.p99) - x(b.p50)} height="14" rx="2" fill={`${b.tone}29`} />
							<path d={`M${x(b.p99)} ${yc - 9} V${yc + 9}`} stroke={b.tone} stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="2 2" />
							<rect x={x(b.p50) - 1.5} y={yc - 11} width="3" height="22" rx="1" fill={b.tone} />
							<text x="160" y={b.t + 58} font-size="9.5" fill="#6E7480">
								{b.foot}
							</text>
							<text x="696" y={yc} font-size="10.5" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central">
								<tspan fill="#F2EFEA" font-weight="600">{b.p50}</tspan>
								<tspan fill="#5A606C"> / </tspan>
								<tspan fill="#8C919B">{b.p99}</tspan>
							</text>
						</g>
					);
				})
			}

			<g>
				<text x="0" y={wifi.t + 22} font-size="11" font-weight="600" fill="#F2EFEA">Wi-Fi 6</text>
				<text x="0" y={wifi.t + 36} font-size="9.5" fill="#8C919B">direct UDP · 1360 B</text>
				<text x="160" y={wifi.t + 13} font-size="9" fill="#6E7480">min RTT not published</text>
				<rect x={x(wifi.lo)} y={wc - 7} width={x(wifi.hi) - x(wifi.lo)} height="14" rx="2" fill="#F2C94C29"></rect>
				<rect x={x(wifi.lo) - 1.5} y={wc - 11} width="3" height="22" rx="1" fill="#F2C94C"></rect>
				<rect x={x(wifi.hi) - 1.5} y={wc - 11} width="3" height="22" rx="1" fill="#F2C94C"></rect>
				<text x={x(wifi.hi) + 8} y={wc + 3} font-size="9" fill="#F2C94C">p50 range</text>
				<text x="160" y={wifi.t + 58} font-size="9.5" fill="#6E7480">about +4 ms median vs wired · idle ICMP 3–295 ms (power save)</text>
				<text x="696" y={wc} font-size="10.5" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central">
					<tspan fill="#F2EFEA" font-weight="600">4.4 – 8.4</tspan>
					<tspan fill="#5A606C"> / —</tspan>
				</text>
			</g>
		</svg>
	</div>
	<figcaption>
		Wired direct UDP is the reference path. Tailscale costs about 0.15 ms of extra minimum RTT and 60 bytes
		per packet, and its tails get long enough that Planck caps it at 100 Mbps direct. Wi-Fi costs about
		4 ms of median latency before anything else happens.
	</figcaption>
	<p class="chart__method">
		<b>Rig</b> bigboi (Windows 11) → M5 Pro (macOS 27.0) · <b>Wired</b> Thunderbolt 2.5GbE; the Wi-Fi 6
		figures measure the Mac's Wi-Fi downlink · <b>Mode</b> raw AEAD UDP burst, 1100-byte shards on the
		wired and Tailscale comparison at 100 Mbps, 1360-byte shards on the congestion-control matrix that
		gives the Wi-Fi range, no induced loss · <b>Tailscale</b> direct WireGuard only: <b>DERP relay was
		never measured</b> · <b>Source</b> <code>docs/spikes/spike3-transport/RESULTS.md</code> lines 10,
		20–27, 55, 73–110 · <b>Commit</b> <code>v0.1.0</code> (<code>8a3c732</code>). Repo guidance: prefer
		direct UDP; treat Tailscale as a fallback at a lower ceiling (<code>RESULTS.md:29</code>).
	</p>
</figure>
